ser":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T16:55:12-08:00","id":21977,"title":"","content":"Why not? I'm busy over the next few days. I'll PM you what I've got. You could offer suggestions and critique if you don't like what I've done, - you may not agree with my core conceits - or help me flesh 'em out more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T19:28:24-08:00","id":26921,"title":"","content":"Well<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-XBlX-LUOl6djJQVkpLYXl1dDQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here's Humanity.</a><br /> Many thanks to Verge, Eremite, DataWeaver and whoever I left out for helping me put this together.<br /> Still looking for suggested adoptions. Please write the level you think they should be at if you have any? Also if you think any should be shifted over to Suggested please feel free to discuss ^^<br /> I'm pretty set on these as a baseline.<br /> <br /> When I say &quot;Tormented&quot; as a Condition I mean Eremite's excellent Conditions. I'm open to new Conditions too, of course; I made &quot;Paranoid&quot; a while ago but it's more Changeling-Mage I feel. I'd love, now that I think we all have more GMC play time under our belts, to get some new stuff written up.<br /> <br /> I'll be starting a &quot;Let's Play&quot; thread in the near future still. As soon as I can have my players back (And Lo, Those Who Work Retail shall be Miserable).<br /> <br /> Also I dunno why I never posted the other stuff as GoogleDocs. So much cleaner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":". 12-10-2013, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T13:41:41-08:00","id":27486,"title":"","content":"Bump for <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-XBlX-LUOl6ellkbzhuU1dJeE0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Beacons.</a> Please let me know what you think, I added a resolution system for them as well and I feel pretty good about it right now, but that's probably because I just wrote it.<br /> Updated Burdens, new Conditions, and then I think the XP table and Beat/Vitriol notes.<br /> Resolving Beacons sounds hella fun to me, by the way. It involves a roll, and I think I owe that to DataWeaver. Thanks again everybody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T22:25:18-08:00","id":27773,"title":"","content":"Annnnd <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-XBlX-LUOl6ZEc2TEcyaDIxRG8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Burden Bump</a>. This is just the overview.<br /> Are the links not working for anyone?<br /> I'll post the actual sample Burdens - tonight? Tonight or tomorrow. Soon. Ish. I want to go over them again since it's been a while.<br /> Finally getting a Promethean PC banged out tonight with somebody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T03:20:27-08:00","id":27861,"title":"","content":"I'm not too keen on the idea of starting with one burden and gaining others in play. I think that Burdens should be something you're created with and loose bit by bit as you become more human. Gaining burdens should be an option, but it should be a significant step backwards rather than typical. I'm also not too keen on the way you've set up resolutions. It seems almost like you have to dodge the easy solutions in order to hold out for the good solutions. I'd prefer that resolving a Burden is always great or even better.<br /> <br /> <br /> Beacons on the other hand look like a good revision of Milestones that tie in the idea of Frankenstein's monster's few positive human contacts to be a big and important thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T08:28:58-08:00","id":27991,"title":"","content":"So I assume you've read the archived thread Verge posted?<br /> <br /> I disagree pretty strongly about Burdens (obviously).<br /> Starting with a bunch - or one big enough to shed gradually - I feel would quickly over-penalize the player. Burdens replace Milestones in these hacks, that's why they have the structued resolutions and are obstacles you encounter instead of assumed issues - they are how you develop Vitriol. I also am not sure how you dodge around the minor ones. The minor ones are the easy way out - learning the hard way. You'll still get Vitriol, but it won't be as satisfying as options which require more effort.<br /> <br /> Some sample Burdens are in the archived thread. I'll be posting them again after work tonight.<br /> <br /> Beacons are the Touchstone analogue. I thought that was obvious? It's worth noting we have very different definitions of Burdens, and I'm not found of starting with them heavy.<br /> That is bad.<br /> Player's don't need *another* reason to find Prometheans difficult at gen. Better to build gradually.<br /> I think the overarching mechanical effect I'll use is that as your Humanity rises, your Burdens get less painful. Sort of like Banes.<br /> <br /> For the record (as the internet will show, somewhere, like in the above-mentioned thread I believe), I initially had Burdens as another set of Aspirations, by the way, months and months and months ago, but DataWeaver and Verge sold me on this model. I still consider the other one, though there'd be less Bane-like crunch and - I imagine - the Resolutions would look similar to how I have them now, since they're modeled off Milestones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":". 12-11-2013, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T08:32:20-08:00","id":27996,"title":"","content":"Also, sorry if I sound curt. Gurrrilla writing at work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T08:54:26-08:00","id":28008,"title":"","content":"I haven't read the archive thread.<br /> <br /> Beacon's looked like a combination of Milestones and touchstones because of the ability to resolve them combined with touchstone like benefits; using them as milestones or tying them to milestones also makes perfect sense. Vampire touch stones are things you hold onto as you slide down and loose humanity. Eventually your grip is going to fail. For Prometheans beacons are things you walk towards as you move towards humanity, eventually you're going to walk past them.<br /> <br /> <br /> For Burdens, I think that once thing that needs to be done with GMC is to tone down Wasteland a lot and simplify Disquiet. That would ease a lot of the pressure and leave room for starting burdens. More to the point though, gaining and removing burdens just doesn't fit the metaphor of the pilgrimage that well.<br /> <br /> Every Pilgrimage has it's ups and downs, but the overall trajectory is (hopefully) up. In other words, your lowest point is usually at the very start, so that's when you should have the most Burdens. Even with the severity of Burden's tied to Humanity, the number of Burdens is the thing that's going to have the emotive weight behind it so having more burdens several months in than at the very start is going to feel all wrong. Changing it so that Promethains start with 3 Burdens and leaving everything else pretty much the same would fix that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally Resolutions. You say that you modelled them on Milestones, but there's one major difference. For a milestone you could fail or you could succeed and every success was awesome. Here you have the idea of minor successes which almost seem to be the default and are barely a success at all, I think that's a problem since it detracts from resolutions which should be a big and very good thing.<br /> <br /> Rather than saying there's a bad, good and best solution to every problem you should do what Milestones did and base the Vitriol on the difficulty of the problem.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. It would be a lot easier to read your posts with paragraph breaks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-11-2013, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T09:03:49-08:00","id":28014,"title":"","content":"My phone is eating my paragraph breaks. Will edit later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T09:04:30-08:00","id":28016,"title":"","content":"That makes sense <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T15:48:01-08:00","id":30627,"title":"","content":"You will note I did not post as promised. I apologize for that; here's why:<br /> <br /> 1. I slept forever<br /> 2. I then proceeded to work forever<br /> 3. Verge has managed to, through some kind of great irony, point out that mechanical Burdens may be a bad idea.<br /> <br /> Now, I've thought this forever; I thought &quot;Burdens as a second set of Aspirations&quot; was totally where it was at to begin with, and now I'm looking at that model again.<br /> <br /> TKR, lemme respond to you in full now:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I haven't read the archive thread. </div> </div> </div>This saddens me. Most of this is in there.<br /> Lemme tell you what changed real quick:<br /> 1. You can refine Beacons now.<br /> 2. Humanity is cleaner and better fleshed-out.<br /> <br /> The Burdens are in there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beacon's looked like a combination of Milestones and touchstones because of the ability to resolve them combined with touchstone like benefits; using them as milestones or tying them to milestones also makes perfect sense. Vampire touch stones are things you hold onto as you slide down and loose humanity. Eventually your grip is going to fail. For Prometheans beacons are things you walk towards as you move towards humanity, eventually you're going to walk past them. </div> </div> </div>I disagree with &quot;walking past them,&quot; unless &quot;things I want to include within myself when I'm finally done with this Pilgrimage&quot; is part of that.<br /> You aspire to be human. Beacons are part of that, and the resolution of them was never meant to represent walking past them; it's meant to represent coming to terms and incorporating it into yourself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For Burdens, I think that once thing that needs to be done with GMC is to tone down Wasteland a lot and simplify Disquiet. That would ease a lot of the pressure and leave room for starting burdens. More to the point though, gaining and removing burdens just doesn't fit the metaphor of the pilgrimage that well. </div> </div> </div>Verge has already done something like that, but yes, Disquiet needs to be simplified. I don't think Wasteland needs to be toned down, I think it needs to be easier to use, and I think some changes on a basic level (like Verge did with his simplified hacks, which are seriously very very good), will make it less painful both to use and to have occur.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every Pilgrimage has it's ups and downs, but the overall trajectory is (hopefully) up. In other words, your lowest point is usually at the very start, so that's when you should have the most Burdens. Even with the severity of Burden's tied to Humanity, the number of Burdens is the thing that's going to have the emotive weight behind it so having more burdens several months in than at the very start is going to feel all wrong. Changing it so that Promethains start with 3 Burdens and leaving everything else pretty much the same would fix that. </div> </div> </div>Ok.<br /> So first, I very consciously decided picking up Burdens was a fine thing, because even though it makes the Pilgrimage seem strange and like a bad metaphor, always having a Burden means you're always locked into the Pilgrimage - it's the psychological fear of change, even though the thing you want most is change.<br /> I, obviously, see how it can be a weird to pick them up in-play. Making them the mechanic by which someone gains Humanity was something I was torn about, but forumites asked for it so I drafted this stuff up with that in mind.<br /> <br /> Now, initially, they were Aspiration-like, and then Bane-like. I think if I were to keep them Bane-like, it *would* be o-k to have a Promethean - as an optional - pick them up upon failing Degeneration instead of losing Humanity. It is back-slidy, but losing Humanity is the *ultimnate* back-slide on the Pilgrimage, and having it turn out that &quot;your Burden is still very real and you are not as far along as you thought&quot; or &quot;You have gone in the wrong direction on the Pilgrimage&quot; sounds fine to me. The metaphor is maintained; you can get lost on the road.<br /> <br /> I'm still leery of letting the Promethean start with three. From an Aspirations/Obsessions stand-point, this may be bad, because it removes the ability to say &quot;this is cool and I want it to be a Burden.&quot; From a mechanical stand point, this *is* bad, because it is over-penalizing the player (yes, if Disquiet and Wasteland are toned down it should be easier to account for Burdens and their associated complications, but they aren't right now).<br /> <br /> Now, if I were to remove the mechanic aspect and *just* make them Aspiration/Obsession analogues: sure, you can start with three, and then they're basically player-chosen Milestones. This was my original idea!<br /> I dunno if I like it.<br /> <br /> Honestly, seeing the stuff Verge is doing with Anchors/Refinements and the like, I'm leaning towards removing the concept of Burdens all-together: you don't want Burdens that don't Burden (DataWeaver to thank for that), and you don't want to over-tax the player at gen, so. There's probably a better thing to replace them with.<br /> <br /> I'm still down with gradually building Humanity. That shit sounds fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally Resolutions. You say that you modelled them on Milestones, but there's one major difference. For a milestone you could fail or you could succeed and every success was awesome. Here you have the idea of minor successes which almost seem to be the default and are barely a success at all, I think that's a problem since it detracts from resolutions which should be a big and very good thing.<br /> <br /> Rather than saying there's a bad, good and best solution to every problem you should do what Milestones did and base the Vitriol on the difficulty of the problem. </div> </div> </div>...but there is a bad/good/best solution to every problem. Sometimes the best solution is depressing and sometimes the bad solution is awful, but that's how life is. I firmly disagree here.<br /> More relevant: since you haven't looked at the old thread, and you're only basing this response off of the write-up example, let me post five Burdens here so you can look at them. It occurred to me that the explanations of the resolutions were somewhat off-putting.<br /> It's not &quot;bad.&quot; It's &quot;the easy way out.&quot;<br /> The &quot;best&quot; just means you tried harder to get it.<br /> <br /> Here's as they are on the old thread. Again, less-mechanic-y Burdens have been on my mind for a while: especially because, since you're keen on having the Promethean start with a bunch and then shedding them, would mean that they're less punishing (presumably, anyway) and would therefore be easier to work into a starting character.<br /> I'm (obviously) into the idea of Prometheans picking up Burdens/losing an adopted Breaking Point when they fail a Degeneration roll instead of losing Humanity; backsliding.<br /> <br /> <b>Unwilling Organ </b><br /> One of your limbs moves on its own, regardless of your will. Whenever you are in a stressful situation, roll (Resolve + Composure); if you fail, the offending limbs does everything possible to trip you up, and you gain the appropriate Arm or Leg Wrack Tilt for the duration of the event.<br /> <b>Resolution Suggestions:</b> You bind the limb to your body with straps and bandages (Minor); You cut off the limb and replace it with one appropriate to your Lineage (Major); You discover who this particular limb belonged to (Superlative)<br /> <br /> <b>Daemon Incarnate </b><br /> Though you seek to become human, you are not; you are far worse, and the pure, as well as the faithful, can tell. Any human with Integrity 8 or higher <i>or</i> who is affiliated with a religion or faith treats your Azoth as two higher for the purposes of generating Disquiet.<br /> <b>Resolution Suggestions:</b> Defy those who judge you by burning their place of worship to the ground (Minor); Seek to join a religious group and successfully do so (Major); Figure out what kind of fiend they take you for and prove them wrong (Superlative)<br /> <br /> <b>Hellbent</b><br /> You are driven to make another suffer. Whether a Beacon who spurned you, a dire enemy, or your own creator, you will not rest until they have felt the fullness of your wrath. You suffer from the Obsession Condition, focused on making a single individual suffer endlessly for a slight (small or large; real or perceived).<br /> <b>Resolution Suggestions:</b> The target dies (Minor); You destroy everything they have ever built and burn their legacy to the ground (Major); You realize that causing them suffering has only intensified your own, and seek to make whatever restitution possible (Superlative)<br /> <br /> <b>The Horrors I\u2019ve Seen </b><br /> It\u2019s not that you\u2019re unhinged, really; just that you\u2019ve seen a little too much of the dark world, of the things man was not meant to know. This has shocked you, and made you unsteady in your Pilgrimage. You suffer from the Mute Condition.<br /> <b>Resolution Suggestions:</b> Embrace the monstrous and learn any Pandoran Transmutation (Minor); Destroy what has traumatized you (Major); Find someone who can both resist your Disquiet and share the terrible weight of your knowledge (Superlative)<br /> <br /> <b>Haunted</b><br /> Nobody wants to be hounded and tormented by restless souls, by ghosts of the dead. Unfortunately, your opinion on the matter doesn\u2019t count. Whether the previous owners of your body or victims of your Torment, ghosts haunt you. You count as an Anchor for your ghostly pursuers, and have the Anchor Condition. It\u2019s also fairly easy for them to make the area around you Open; if you suffer a Dramatic Failure, apply the Open Condition to an area around you equal to (Azoth x3) yards in radius, applying for all ghosts Anchored to you.<br /> <b>Resolution Suggestions:</b> Dig up and burn their bodies (Minor); Find an exorcist willing to help you, even though Disquiet makes them think you deserve it (Major); Resolve whatever drives these ghosts and put them to rest (Superlative)<br /> <br /> <b>That Terrible Light</b><br /> Your Azoth burns brightly; terribly, awfully bright. Treat your Azoth as three higher for the purposes of Azothic Radience. This notably counts for other Prometheans sensing you and for awakening Pandorans.<br /> <b>Resolution Suggestions:</b> Shuff the light off onto another Promethean, inflicting them with this Burden \u2013 this counts as a Lacunae for mechanics, though it provides no Vitriol and requires you to net 10 successes (Minor); Cleanse yourself by entering the Wastes and dropping your Azoth a dot \u2013 this leaves a permanent, 20-mile Wasteland there, which glows eerily at night (Major); Raise all the Pandorans, fiends and monsters in a city and proceed to cleanse the heck out of it (Superlative)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":". 12-15-2013, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T23:18:28-08:00","id":32192,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have a link to the stuff BHM did on rpg.net? I wasn't following closely because i never absorbed the G-M rules until the final product came out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T02:47:07-08:00","id":32248,"title":"","content":"Hey Ben, thank's for the reply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/7219-house-ruled-promethean-gmc-patches?p=30627#post30627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree with &quot;walking past them,&quot; unless &quot;things I want to include within myself when I'm finally done with this Pilgrimage&quot; is part of that.<br /> You aspire to be human. Beacons are part of that, and the resolution of them was never meant to represent walking past them; it's meant to represent coming to terms and incorporating it into yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div> Good news: We actually agree.<br /> <br /> &quot;Coming to terms and incorporating it into yourself&quot; was pretty much what I meant. Let's say your Beacon is dog-tags from whomever's body you are made from. One day you find out about how you died and learn an important lesson.<br /> <br /> That lesson will always be with you and it's part of the human you will one day become, but at the same time you cannot learn <i>anything more</i> from those dog-tags. That's what I mean by you having &quot;walked past&quot; the dog tags.<br /> <br /> <br /> So first, I very consciously decided picking up Burdens was a fine thing, because even though it makes the Pilgrimage seem strange and like a bad metaphor, always having a Burden means you're always locked into the Pilgrimage - it's the psychological fear of change, even though the thing you want most is change.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/7219-house-ruled-promethean-gmc-patches?p=30627#post30627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, obviously, see how it can be a weird to pick them up in-play. Making them the mechanic by which someone gains Humanity was something I was torn about, but forumites asked for it so I drafted this stuff up with that in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div> I've got a question. Why not make Beacons the mechanic by which someone gains humanity?<br /> <br /> The way I would do it is that beacons are the primary way of advancing to Humanity.<br /> <br /> Burdens would be just flat disadvantages, much like the weakness to fire. When you resolve a Beacon you, if it's fitting, remove one Burden or lesson the severity of a Burden. This represents some aspect of your Promethian nature is being replaced with a more human equivalent.<br /> <br /> You get beats from Burdens, but that's not so much a representation of how they help you on the Pilgramage but an OOC disadvantages -&gt; beats rule. Though mind you, it could (especially in the early game) do quite well as being the OOC rule for the IC bit where Promethians learn like sponges during their early life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/7219-house-ruled-promethean-gmc-patches?p=30627#post30627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, initially, they were Aspiration-like, and then Bane-like. I think if I were to keep them Bane-like, it *would* be o-k to have a Promethean - as an optional - pick them up upon failing Degeneration instead of losing Humanity. It is back-slidy, but losing Humanity is the *ultimnate* back-slide on the Pilgrimage, and having it turn out that &quot;your Burden is still very real and you are not as far along as you thought&quot; or &quot;You have gone in the wrong direction on the Pilgrimage&quot; sounds fine to me. The metaphor is maintained; you can get lost on the road.</div> </div> </div> </div> This works for me, though I'd probably use a dice mechanic rather than a choice mechanic like Vampire. Basically when you loose Humanity roll your new Humanity to see if you gain a Burden.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/7219-house-ruled-promethean-gmc-patches?p=30627#post30627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still down with gradually building Humanity. That shit sounds fun.</div> </div> </div> </div> Me too, but I'd remove the bit about Promethians trying to cheat the system with easy to adhere too rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/7219-house-ruled-promethean-gmc-patches?p=30627#post30627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but there is a bad/good/best solution to every problem. Sometimes the best solution is depressing and sometimes the bad solution is awful, but that's how life is. I firmly disagree here.</div> </div> </div> </div> Let me step back a bit.<br /> <br /> It seems like a lot of the easiest solutions you promise are so easy that a PC would have to intentionally avoid them to ever get a chance to reach the good solution. Take Unwilling Organ. I can't imagine anyone not binding the limb just as a place-holder while they go on a quest to discover who this particular limb belonged to. It's not the idea that there's a bad/good/best solution so much as the way you're handling the split. (Also, I'd kinda prefer fail/ok/good/best to bad/good/best)<br /> <br /> <br /> A better way would be to think of a climactic moment in which all options are possible. So for Unwilling Organ: The Climactic Moment is &quot;you find out who this limb belonged to&quot;, and you can solve that moment by:<br /> <br /> Fail: You don't realise you're looking at your arm's old owner.<br /> Ok: You realise that your former life means little to you, putting the past in the past quiets your arm for good.<br /> Good: You feel a sense of moral responsibility to finish some of your arm's former owner's unfinished business but not any personal connection. Finishing the business quiets the arm and teaches you a basic lesson about humanity like &quot;due to the dead&quot;.<br /> Best: You feel that your existence is a continuation of the dead guy and resolve his business for both moral and personal reasons. Making a dead human's life part of your own makes you quite a bit more human.<br /> <br /> <br /> BTW as I said above, I like the idea that resolving Beacons fixes burdens. In this case some clue to your arm's former owner could be the Beacon that resolves your arm. Alternatively the arm could be both a Burden (it's a problem) and a Beacon (your drive to fix it helps you on the pilgrimage). A counter example would be a Promethian with Hellbent against their Creator and a Beacon - a photo - of someone else who will teach them an important lesson about forgiveness and fix Hellbent even though there's no direct link between the two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-19-2013, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T18:28:15-08:00","id":32885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/7219-house-ruled-promethean-gmc-patches?p=32192#post32192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have a link to the stuff BHM did on rpg.net? I wasn't following closely because i never absorbed the G-M rules until the final product came out.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?676474-Promethean-The-Created-updated-with-GMC\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...dated-with-GMC</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom"